        "id": 5603,
        "name": "lugaru",
        "username": "lugaru",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lugaru/{size}/2767_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-04-12T14:16:49.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hey, just bought the game and expansion at PAX EAST, after a fun demo using Legacy.</p>\n<p>I’m running a few games this Saturday, so I have not had a chance to do an official game yet, but I’m really looking forward to it.</p>\n<p>That said opening a massive box of cards is a little maddening, and I’m still trying to decide exactly how to organize it all.</p>\n<p>So I was wondering: how about for future “small” expansions putting out deck boxes? I dont just mean like a big box with a ton of tinnier boxes in it… but I mean micro expansions.</p>\n<p>Something like a “Nemesis Pack” where you could have (as generic as possible) Captain Good (41 card deck) vs Major Evil (22 card villain deck) in a nice old fasioned cardboard deck box. Seems like a cheap and fun way to keep expanding the universe, and easier to store.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:35:18.088Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
