      {
        "id": 27183,
        "name": "EvanDan55",
        "username": "EvanDan55",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/evandan55/{size}/2374_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-04-12T20:59:34.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;Spiff&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"Spiff\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I’d buy a Nemesis Pack, although I’d like it to include a new environment as well.</p>\n<p>In fact, maybe SotM expansions could be like World of Warcraft expansion – we get a major expansion (Rook City), then a few months later we get a new hero/villain/environment that goes with Rook City, then a few months later we get another, etc.  Heck, things could even build with each expansion the way they do with WoW so that the final Nemesis Pack in the Rook City line could have included The Chairman, making him the ultimate boss of the cycle.  I’d pay money for that.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I kinda like that idea, but at the same time, I like having a set time for when essentially every part of an expansion comes out. I’d of course be okay with adding onto the expansions, if new ideas that would fit perfectly came up after the expansion. But I like getting everything at once.</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:01:09.269Z",
