      {
        "id": 27185,
        "name": "Rabit",
        "username": "Rabit",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-04-12T22:48:28.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;Christopher&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"Christopher\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Our next major release as a company will involve a storage solution.  But more on that next week!</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Awesome!  ;D I’ll definitely be looking forward to that.</p>\n<p>A little more feedback for consideration: (Unfortunately, there’s always different opinions - &gt;G is going to have to do the marketting analysis and find a way to get the greatest bang for their buck! <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=12\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> )</p>\n<p>One of the things I like about Rook City is the cohesive flavor of the set. While Matriarch is a little outside of this (she could have come from anywhere), the rest of the set is beautifully cohesive, thematically. Artistically, the entire set is impressively cohesive. (Birds everywhere! 8) ) For me, that’s a very big part of my enjoyment of the game.</p>\n<p>Coming out with individual character decks would be interesting, but I’m not one of the folks who would enjoy that as much as themed set.</p>\n<p>My biggest suggestion for future expansions: Keep 'em coming! Luckily, I don’t see that as being an issue. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=12\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>Rabit</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:01:09.384Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 1,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.2,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 5601,
        "topic_slug": "advice-for-future-expansions-decks",
